  "implementation": [
    "One fixed current-30 operator and a PowerShell launcher. They consume externally pinned owner approval and separate original 24/six grants; there is no issuer, limit increase, account purchase, replacement ledger or generic authorization service.",
    "Default PowerShell without packet arguments performs only hidden-input account inspection via fixed GET /api/v1/key. It retains only selected non-secret metadata and the credential SHA in a bounded terminal summary, including an insufficient-current-cap diagnosis. It does not require or manufacture fee approval, UI account evidence or a startup slot.",
    "Packet CheckOnly remains read-only; ExecuteApproved requires the owner-approved digest, shared two-hour window, current candidate/packet/source/docs/request/config pins, credential binding, independently reviewed Credits/guardrail record and separate unused startup slots.",
    "Exact key source number lexemes are parsed conservatively and every enforcement budget checked. Credits are explicitly a whole-dollar lower bound floored from a separately reviewed two-decimal UI display, not an exact Credits API amount. Evidence must be at most 15 minutes old at startup; its hash/account/key binding is pinned externally. No /credits endpoint, management credential or UI scraping is used.",
    "Existing 24 runner/journal/capture and six private collector/SQLite/export do all accounting. Denial-only hooks run before sent/markSending and release local refusals without unknown-paid accounting. Six's live bridge fixes the real transport, ledger path and source verifier; fixtures remain offline-only.",
    "The existing supplement ledger identity and collecting/held state are read-only checked before 24 and again before six. Complete captures, verified unique settled receipts, zero held cost and a fresh key allowance are required to start six. Settled quality failures remain captured and scored without retry.",
    "Source/body/window guards run at each inference handoff. The provider retains its existing one POST and up-to-three generation GET bounds. Private approval/output permissions use owner/SYSTEM/admin SID checks; plaintext secrets never enter arguments, persisted configuration or summaries. Fixed refusal codes replace raw upstream errors."
  ],
